### Cohort invariants

Sequential attrition must never increase N.

No patient may occupy two mutually exclusive treatment arms at the same decision time.

A treatment episode classified NON_HCC cannot enter an HCC line of therapy.

### Temporal invariants

Baseline variables must precede the treatment-decision index.

Outcome events cannot precede index.

Same-regimen maintenance must not become a new line.

Restarting the same treatment after a temporary hold must not automatically become a new line.

### Clinical cadence invariants

Check median treatment intervals against plausible clinical schedules.

Flag:
- median interval <5 days for q3–4 week therapy
- implausibly high duplicate daily orders
- combination components occurring months apart but classified as one regimen

Every failed invariant must be printed.

